cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ctbench: a matched-pair constant-time RTL benchmark and reference checker"
message: "If you use this corpus or checker in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: nickharris808
    website: "https://github.com/nickharris808"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickharris808/ctbench"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nickh007/hw-verify"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark corpus and reference checker for constant-time properties of RTL. Every
  safe design ships beside a leaky twin with an identical interface, so a tool earns a
  pair only by separating both halves; an out-of-remit control is genuinely
  constant-time and functionally wrong, so a tool that flags it is recorded as crying
  wolf. Scoring ranks soundness first: a tool that reports one leaky design safe ranks
  below every sound tool regardless of accuracy. The checker returns a third verdict,
  UNKNOWN, for designs it cannot read, rather than reporting an unanalysed design as
  safe.
keywords:
  - constant-time
  - side-channel
  - hardware security
  - verilog
  - benchmark
  - formal verification
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-28"
